<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:04:04Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Watch live: Trump holds press conference after meeting with Xi, Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f09b6e0d252c69af3b24011c853ac1edf2dd87b70075af44e5a11adefc802070</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T16:30:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-watch-live-trump-holds-press-conference-meeting-xi-putin--de6586fb5a55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-watch-live-trump-holds-press-conference-meeting-xi-putin" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump is set to hold a White House press conference Friday, following his return to Washington after a four-day trip to Asia that saw him sit down for a first-ever trilateral meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin. Watch his conference live from 11:30am EST (5:30pm Paris time).</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Jamaica's beaches are increasingly off limits to locals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e64873b27d588c9db584014178c65f6224baba3b94329665678cfa0b7c14f2b</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:03:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:55:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261120-jamaica-beaches-off-limits-to-locals-property-developers-hotels--8b1ba04df6ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261120-jamaica-beaches-off-limits-to-locals-property-developers-hotels" /><summary type="html">Jamaica usually conjures up images of white sandy beaches, Rastafari culture and Bob Marley – but another reality exists. On this small Caribbean island, less than 1 percent of the coastline is freely accessible to local people. The rest has gradually been privatised, mostly for large hotel developments and private homes.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>El Salvador: Nayib Bukele, self-proclaimed “coolest dictator on earth”, is seeking a third term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7dc638fc57c038a932d573cee526a669f6b74fc90629e8dbdd625340b5bb019c</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:04:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:07:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-self-proclaimed-coolest-dictator-on-earth-is-seeking-a-third-term--1aebd0b55990.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-self-proclaimed-coolest-dictator-on-earth-is-seeking-a-third-term" /><summary type="html">🇸🇻 El Salvador’s President Nayib Bukele, who calls himself the “coolest dictator on earth”, is seeking a third term after changing the Constitution to scrap presidential term limits. His war on gangs has made him hugely popular, but also sparked serious human rights concerns.</summary></entry><entry><title>White House fires national cyber director over widespread outages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6387e2e253960dbd4c5dd2cb01a331d7d8981111a4fd18502e429984a9bc9c93</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T01:28:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-white-house-fires-national-cyber-director-over-widespread-outages--e5d5af4d4476.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-white-house-fires-national-cyber-director-over-widespread-outages" /><summary type="html">The White House fired national cyber director Sean Cairncross on Thursday following a week of technology disruptions affecting US air travel, email services and national security systems. The departure comes as the Trump administration faces criticism over its response to the outages, which officials say were unrelated incidents.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Armed forces in Haiti kill at least 34 gang members to regain control of key corridor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed7d7a37da62a920f87904d7a0b4abfa7193fada934a4fbbf92b9a22902b2e8d</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T22:31:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261119-major-anti-gang-offensive-in-haiti-kills-34-suspected-gang-members--26a4355e6e18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261119-major-anti-gang-offensive-in-haiti-kills-34-suspected-gang-members" /><summary type="html">Haitian security forces launched a major offensive on Thursday to retake Martissant, a strategic corridor linking Port-au-Prince with the country's western and southern regions that gangs have controlled for five years. Police said at least 34 suspected gang members were killed in clashes involving a private security task force.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>A president among body bags: Photo ops spark outrage in Colombia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19dc3c09d9d7a6ba32dd635620726ee6c8e69c71ed21c80c00c27055c9e378c2</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:52:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261119-president-body-bags-photo-ops-sparking-outrage-colombia--7fdcc25cb912.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261119-president-body-bags-photo-ops-sparking-outrage-colombia" /><summary type="html">Since taking office in August, Colombia's far-right President Abelardo de la Espriella has regularly posted videos that show him walking among body bags supposedly holding the remains of rebel fighters – a communications strategy that has sparked widespread criticism.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>NASA's Voyager 1 phones home from record one light-day away, 49 years after launch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:714cd6db5955704531a871897790fa9989fc5f510fe813f4c3714829be54f8d0</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:26:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nasa-voyager-1-phones-home-from-record-one-light-day-away-49-years-after-launch--ea85baca7960.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nasa-voyager-1-phones-home-from-record-one-light-day-away-49-years-after-launch" /><summary type="html">The Voyager 1 probe launched by NASA nearly a half century ago has reached a distance from Earth of one light day (more than 26 billion kilometres), the farthest any human artifact has ever ventured from our planet. The space agency received a signal from the spacecraft Thursday, exactly 24 hours after it was sent.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Xi, Putin summit: What was it all about?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38bf090f5361b3291ff4e8ed32ce51ec6f29f612e5469c6e06a6522c5877f8be</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:12:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-xi-putin-summit-what-was-it-all-about--2c0baba62b07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-xi-putin-summit-what-was-it-all-about" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has left China after a historic first meeting with Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the APEC summit. Ukraine was discussed without Kyiv or European leaders in the room, which raised eyebrows, though Trump defended dialogue with rivals and Putin said the talks created conditions for future agreements. Xi warned major powers against conflict, and topics included reducing nuclear risks, reforming the UN and increasing energy flows.</summary></entry><entry><title>Haiti: Salvador’s Bukele publishes video of attack on gang leader’s house</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ed2dd89f51c21b51eb153a60ec558a603cc17d5be93c587f509217175afb0d4</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:06:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-haiti-salvador-s-bukele-publishes-video-of-attack-on-gang-leader-s-house--14ac3f8f83f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-haiti-salvador-s-bukele-publishes-video-of-attack-on-gang-leader-s-house" /><summary type="html">Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele said Wednesday that his troops demolished the lavish home of a prominent gang leader in Haiti known as Jeff Gwo Lwa. "My gift to the Haitian people on the anniversary of the Battle of Vertières," Bukele wrote on X - referencing a 1803 battle critical in helping secure Haiti's independence from France.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Democrats nominate Jeffries to be first Black House speaker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9b59ea08d0428d33184f4df9c6982d85682c373a63a4015511f536656511b50</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:58:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-democrats-nominate-jeffries-to-be-first-black-house-speaker--1a82a2206b26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-democrats-nominate-jeffries-to-be-first-black-house-speaker" /><summary type="html">Hakeem Jeffries is on the cusp of becoming the first Black speaker of the US House of Representatives after Democrats elected him their leader Wednesday following a sweeping midterm election triumph. Jeffries faced no declared challenger, although opposition from some newly elected progressives had exposed divisions over how Democrats should wield their newfound power. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hegseth makes surprise trip to Venezuela, renews military cooperation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f569e4f888c51128fc638652113c2a513fe75090d0713cb84773345dcce0dd8</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T18:59:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-hegseth-makes-surprise-trip-to-venezuela-renews-military-cooperation--c69718d51c80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-hegseth-makes-surprise-trip-to-venezuela-renews-military-cooperation" /><summary type="html">US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth made an unannounced visit to Caracas on Wednesday, announcing a resumption of military cooperation with Venezuela and vowing to crack down on drug traffickers. The trip marks the highest-level US visit since the ouster of Nicolas Maduro in January, signalling a dramatic shift in relations between the two countries.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Beijing has supported Moscow but 'China understands that America is way more important than Russia'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a519af091d54a71d0c572e4be7115b931d4c4adcb8df358d076047d087dab324</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T17:48:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia--f9f88efc8e97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia" /><summary type="html">Following Xi Jinping's very friendly rare tarmac greeting for Donald Trump, Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Kerry Brown, Professor of Chinese Studies and Director of the Lau China Institute at King's College, London. Brown examines the complex relationship between the world's two largest economies, China's growing diplomatic influence and the competition over artificial intelligence.“China is the diplomatic center of the world,” says Brown, pointing to Beijing's ability to bring together leaders from Russia, the United States, Europe and elsewhere. He argues that China now has “extraordinary convening power" and significant influence over Russia.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Democrats nominate Hakeem Jeffries to be first Black speaker of the House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e5a98dfd003f4ff8091f890f16f87e17a9441a0b2205523b9f8d82e4b1579c5</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:44:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-us-democrats-nominate-hakeem-jeffries-to-be-first-black-speaker-of-the-house--380c6ed3ece3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-us-democrats-nominate-hakeem-jeffries-to-be-first-black-speaker-of-the-house" /><summary type="html">Democrats nominated Hakeem Jeffries on Wednesday to be the next speaker of the House of Representatives, putting him on track to make history as the nation’s first Black American with the gavel.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Peltola defeats Sullivan in Alaska Senate race, expanding Democratic majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecf636887c0f5e76289aea59380fce64ab6913e47d9e91c28288086393ea1ddf</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T03:47:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-peltola-defeats-sullivan-in-alaska-senate-race-expanding-democratic-majority--a4d690c354ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-peltola-defeats-sullivan-in-alaska-senate-race-expanding-democratic-majority" /><summary type="html">Democrat Mary Peltola defeated Republican Sen. Dan Sullivan in Alaska on Tuesday, completing a political comeback in a state that US President Donald Trump has repeatedly won by wide margins. Her victory gives Democrats a 56-44 Senate majority, marking their biggest net gain in Senate seats since 1958.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Haitians rally behind Bukele as Salvadoran troops battle gangs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bef17d4bb5a7a912e7fb2d123755bdbd36774ae0da44d6737ddeedace39312c7</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T02:42:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-haitians-rally-behind-bukele-as-salvadoran-troops-battle-gangs--576572e0300d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-haitians-rally-behind-bukele-as-salvadoran-troops-battle-gangs" /><summary type="html">Thousands of Haitians took to the streets on Tuesday to urge El Salvador's President Nayib Bukele to keep fighting gangs, as his troops bolster security forces in the Caribbean nation. But experts warn that growing public support could turn to anger without a long-term plan to tackle violence and strengthen Haiti's police.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US, Mexico and Bolivia lose measles-free status as deaths mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a3c4ad7aff6e39376edd37b4e29607a9a275e64225dc359c416f733fe6e0c56</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T21:30:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-us-mexico-and-bolivia-lose-measles-free-status-as-deaths-mount--3ecebbb665bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-us-mexico-and-bolivia-lose-measles-free-status-as-deaths-mount" /><summary type="html">The US has lost its measles-free status, international health officials said Tuesday, as the highly contagious virus has spread at the fastest rate in more than 30 years, while Mexico and Bolivia also lost their measles-elimination status. Vaccination rates have been falling against a number of diseases, in the US and globally, and measles has been spreading throughout the Americas since 2024.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Iran 'playing mind games with the United States', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:490c4cd3de511871dafe06e8fc73d1289f3a75f23a583de12a0c2e113ab6aab8</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T20:28:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-playing-mind-games-with-the-united-states-expert-says--5ddc4f0f722f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-playing-mind-games-with-the-united-states-expert-says" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump said Tuesday that US authorities take "very seriously" any possible threat to Washington, following reports Iran was planning to target officials, possibly with a radioactive bomb. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Stimson Center in Washington, says that Iran may be "playing mind games with the United States as a way perhaps of deterring President Trump from unleashing a massive new attack on Iran".</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says he takes possible Iran bomb threat to Washington 'very seriously'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3cc3cd246af440e0d9bf67b9fa687cdad4b6c127247b60a93925c841fa36d51</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T15:44:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-trump-says-he-takes-possible-iran-bomb-threat-to-washington-very-seriously--b7da002abc8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-trump-says-he-takes-possible-iran-bomb-threat-to-washington-very-seriously" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump said Tuesday that US authorities take any possible threats to Washington ‘very seriously’, following reports that Iran was planning to target senior Trump administration officials, possibly with a radioactive bomb.  Tehran dismissed the reports as ‘fabricated’.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Chase outage disrupts US online banking, Zelle payments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c17cd578c5378be69ac433dfd0f8d5e92b308d1867eb06c06f5f9f2b3da12483</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:40:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-chase-outage-disrupts-online-banking-and-zelle-payments-in-united-states-us-software--69cbbbd1d139.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-chase-outage-disrupts-online-banking-and-zelle-payments-in-united-states-us-software" /><summary type="html">Users of several major US banking apps and online portals reported outages on Monday, according to the monitoring site Downdetector.com, with one institution ruling out a cyberattack as the cause. Among those affected by the outages were Bank of America, JPMorgan Chase and the popular money transfer app Zelle.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says he needs funding for air traffic control after ground stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a8481a74613af8998a26ace91a20ef874ba5d957686b5913ce081dd4d4f891f</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:01:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-says-he-needs-funding-for-air-traffic-control-after-ground-stop--48f92ae1d591.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-says-he-needs-funding-for-air-traffic-control-after-ground-stop" /><summary type="html">US ​President ​Donald Trump, pressed on a ​technology ‌failure ⁠that ‌grounded thousands of ⁠flights last week, ​on ‌Monday told reporters ‌that ​the government needed funding for upgrade ​to ​air traffic ​control equipment. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Sheldon Jacobson, Professor of Computer Science at the University of Illinois. He explains that "the Republicans have had full control of the House and the Senate since the President came in. They controlled everything. If they needed the money and wanted the money they could have approved the money. The fact that they didn't, in the the different bills that have been passed, suggests that it's more than just money that is going on here".</summary></entry><entry><title>US judge strikes down Trump visa restrictions on foreign students, journalists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fe006c47f251dc60be90c2848887d4baa1f780d87f7cf22a6c1b03ef419677b</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T21:23:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-us-judge-strikes-down-trump-visa-restrictions-on-foreign-students-journalists--89359086d5e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-us-judge-strikes-down-trump-visa-restrictions-on-foreign-students-journalists" /><summary type="html">A US federal judge struck down a Trump administration policy on Monday that would have sharply limited the length of time foreign students and journalists could stay in the country, ruling that the proposed restrictions were unlawful and would undermine educational opportunity.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>November 17 blackout hoax: How a conspiracy theory went viral around the world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0a3644e8c2b579a591df639c47a5a98b80aedefa0ce138284c7471999ec2835</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:50:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261116-november-17-blackout-hoax-how-a-conspiracy-theory-went-viral-around-the-world--0b2ddebc84cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261116-november-17-blackout-hoax-how-a-conspiracy-theory-went-viral-around-the-world" /><summary type="html">A conspiracy theory claiming a worldwide "blackout" will hit the world on November 17 has spread across social media, with the claim it will cut electricity, internet and banking services. The rumour stems from a routine US FEMA emergency alert test, but was amplified by cryptocurrency accounts, misleading claims about EU preparedness advice and references to "The Simpsons". Recent technology outages, flight disruptions and cyberattacks have added to public anxiety, helping turn a routine test into a global hoax.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Pope concludes South America homecoming, reassures faithful after cancer scare</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18622000feac15032e3d84c9bae081dd11f2f684d8a80f8bfb2bb1359461c3ad</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:50:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-pope-concludes-south-america-homecoming-reassures-faithful-after-cancer-scare--0f38c5877379.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261116-pope-concludes-south-america-homecoming-reassures-faithful-after-cancer-scare" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV finished Monday his 12-day tour of Uruguay, Argentina and Peru reiterating his advocacy for social justice, environmental protection and the importance of community. Just a month after undergoing lung cancer surgery, the 71-year-old pontiff drew millions of faithful across South America, where he spent nearly two decades as a missionary.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>The new faces of the US Congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bee2e145d4db90a84eece66ba04b949318c1cc690eaef0dd5abb7cf215247319</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:36:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-new-faces-of-the-us-congress--c1a20de87eae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-new-faces-of-the-us-congress" /><summary type="html">The United States Congress is about to welcome dozens of new faces. A majority of them, Democratic, after the "blue wave" in the midterm elections. FRANCE 24's Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson catches up with one of these new lawmakers as they go through orientation as they prepare to take office in January. He speaks with Katy Padilla Stout, U.S. Representative-elect for Texas's 23rd congressional district.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mexican drug trade 'boss of bosses' Miguel Angel Felix Gallardo dies at 80</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:617014b314beb549448bdd9a6700790606e94187a3af75c7c2de886ef3f38fbb</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T22:48:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-miguel-angel-felix-gallardo-mexican-drug-lord-dies--90e53724e9b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-miguel-angel-felix-gallardo-mexican-drug-lord-dies" /><summary type="html">Miguel Angel Felix Gallardo, a founder of Mexico’s Guadalajara drug cartel known as the “boss of bosses”, died in hospital on Sunday aged 80 after suffering multiple organ failure, Jalisco state’s security ministry said. Imprisoned since 1989, he had been transferred from prison to the hospital two days before his death.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Record number of women elected' to US Congress &amp; governorships in midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:692dd63ef4f6cc3ebd41ef9585ff73f2aa845c8559884e2cb9bf52e28936a3ad</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:40:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-record-number-of-women-elected-to-us-congress-governorships-across-country-in-midterm-elect--7efef40d71de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-record-number-of-women-elected-to-us-congress-governorships-across-country-in-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Following the 2026 US midterm elections, Gavin Lee welcomes Politico Senior National Politics Reporter Lauren Fedor to discuss the growing number of Democratic women elected to Congress and governorships, particularly mothers of young children.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: The French Connection</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d71bd430e5d2cbee5334a4bfd5e3c2c631dd68a109a78da49b2bd704490bb24</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:03:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-jensen-huang-the-french-connection--c681b71603cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-jensen-huang-the-french-connection" /><summary type="html">President Trump is heading to Asia in a few days' time, where he is due to meet President Putin and President Xi. But there could be one fewer tech giant at the table: Jensen Huang, who has resigned from Nvidia amid a suspected espionage affair.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>US probes nationwide flights stoppage as travel disruptions persist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02d99be26a3a0543b290dba5fc7483bee8f0504e64caaee6f54512d663aacdeb</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:09:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-probes-nationwide-flights-stoppage-as-travel-disruptions-persist--66080e063e19.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-probes-nationwide-flights-stoppage-as-travel-disruptions-persist" /><summary type="html">US air travel is expected to return to normal this Sunday, following a nationwide ground stop Friday night that stranded hundreds of thousands of passengers and disrupted travel worldwide. The Trump administration blamed the incident on a botched replacement of old copper wire communication lines and said there was no evidence this was a cyberattack. The ground stop now raises questions about the country's aging infrastructure and lawmakers are calling for an investigation. Analysis by Philip Mann, aviation expert at Vector Strategic Consulting.</summary></entry><entry><title>Air travel issues persist in the US after nationwide ground stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8567b72872b39c9c7373794b1010e55bde12ba9203bd4c3dbc2312dc9a322aee</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:12:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/air-travel-issues-persist-in-the-us-after-nationwide-ground-stop--ae8922ebd6d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/air-travel-issues-persist-in-the-us-after-nationwide-ground-stop" /><summary type="html">After almost five hours of grounded flights in the US, flights have resumed. However, passengers are still waiting and wading through tough logistics to get to their destinations after massive delays and cancelled flights. Details by Simon Moritz.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope laments poverty-stricken Inca communities as locals leave Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c0653c39cc688ed97b5a6a23a5da38972a8f8d765f82d051679acf195daff37</id><updated>2026-11-20T17:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T10:55:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-laments-poverty-stricken-inca-communities-as-locals-leave-peru--5c41da65bfa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-laments-poverty-stricken-inca-communities-as-locals-leave-peru" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV on Sunday will traverse the length of Peru in what marks the penultimate day of his Latin American tour. The leader of the Catholic church – who underwent cancer surgery just a month ago – warned that Peru's remote Inca communities are under threat as poverty continues to drive locals out of their homeland in search of better futures.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
